{title: Love Letter}
{subtitle: September 2026}
{artist: Kevin Duncan}
{key: D}
{x_flag: unlisted}
{x_theme: blood, grace-mercy, easter, victory}
{x_source: chrd:~love_letter.chrd}

{comment: Intro}
{ci: Solo piano. Sparse, unhurried.}
{ci: This motif is the "voice" of the letter.}
[*d-e-gb-e-gb-e-gb][D]                    [Db]
[*d-e-db-e-gb-g-gb][B]                    [A]
[*gb-e-d-e-d][G]                  [*gb-e-d-e-d][A]                  [*d][D]

{comment: Verse 1}
{ci: Intimate. Almost spoken.}
Before I l[D]it the morning
Or [Db]made stars shine
I [B]had a plan
With [A]you in mind
That [G]someday[A]
For you, for [D]Me
I stretched the [D]sky above you
And c[Db]arved the sea
I [B]held the dust
And [A]breathed you free
[G]Someday you'll[A]
Come home to [D]Me

{comment: Chorus 1}
{ci: Opens up, but stays warm. This is a promise, not a shout.}
This is My l[D]ove letter to y[A]ou
[B]Written by My [A]hand
[G]Sealed with a vow
[A]Before the world be[D]gan
I'm [D]coming back for [A]you
[B]Soon you'll under[A]stand
[G]And you'll know[A]
{ci: (interlude)}
All that I planned

{comment: Interlude 1}
{ci: Same motif, fuller. Hopeful.}
[*d-e-gb-e-gb-e-gb][D]                    [Db]
[*d-e-db-e-gb-g-gb][B]                    [A]
[*gb-e-d-e-d][G]                  [*gb-e-d-e-d][A]                  [*d][D]

{comment: Verse 2}
{ci: Darker. Add tension. Let "ran from grace" ache.}
You wandered [D]from the garden
You [Db]hid your face
You [B]built your walls
You [A]ran from grace
But [G]My love[A]
Would break them d[D]own
I sent My [D]word through prophets
In [Db]every age
I [B]wrote it down
On [A]every page
[G]Someday soon[A]
I'm coming [D]down

{comment: Chorus 2}
{ci: Bigger than Chorus 1.}
This is My l[D]ove letter to y[A]ou
[B]Written by My [A]hand
[G]Sealed with a vow
[A]Before the world be[D]gan
I'm [D]on My way, don't h[A]ide
[B]Soon you'll under[A]stand
[G]And you'll know[A]
{ci: (interlude)}
All that I planned

{comment: Interlude 2}
{ci: Expansive, almost worshipful. The moment before He arrives.}
[*d-e-gb-e-gb-e-gb][D]                    [Db]
[*d-e-db-e-gb-g-gb][B]                    [A]
[*gb-e-d-e-d][G]                  [*gb-e-d-e-d][A]                  [*a][D]
{ci: Again.}
[*d-e-gb-e-gb-e-gb][D]                    [Db]
[*d-e-db-e-gb-g-gb][B]                    [A]
[*gb-e-d-e-d][G]                  [*gb-e-d-e-d][A]                  [*d][D]

{comment: Verse 3}
{ci: Pull back to intimate again, but warmer than Verse 1. He's here.}
I took on [D]skin and heartbeat
A [Db]newborn's cry
I [B]learned to walk
Be[A]neath your sky
[G]Dusty roads[A]
I walked the [D]same
I touched the [D]lepers' faces
I [Db]loved the lost
The [B]last, the least
I [A]knew the cost
I [G]loved you[A]
Called you by [D]name

{comment: Chorus 3}
{ci: Full. Everything in.}
This is My l[D]ove letter to y[A]ou
[B]Written by My [A]hand
[G]Sealed with a vow
[A]Before the world be[D]gan
I'm [D]here with you n[A]ow
[B]Soon you'll under[A]stand
[G]And you'll know[A]
All that I [D]planned

{comment: Bridge}
{ci: Strip everything out. Voice nearly alone.}
{ci: Build slowly through the first half.}
They [B]drove nails in
I [G]did not fight
I [A]saw your face
I [D]held on tight
{ci: Give the vocalist room here.}
[B]Every drop I bled
[G]Ran down the page
{ci: Nearly stop. Let this line hang.}
I [A]signed My name
{ci: THE PEAK. Everything hits.}
[A]Paid sin's [A]full wage
{ci: Hold. Nearly alone. Spoken or on one note.}
[A]It is finished

{comment: Final Chorus}
{ci: Biggest moment of the song. Straight in from the bridge, no gap.}
{ci: Play this part light 1 octave up, but not too bright. Soft vocals.}
This is My l[D]ove letter to y[A]ou
[B]Written by My [A]hand
[G]Sealed with My blood
[A]Before the world be[D]gan
{ci: Walk down to the original octave and gradually intensify.}
I [D]gave it all for y[A]ou
[B]Now you under[A]stand
[G]Now you know[A]
All that I [D]planned

{comment: Outro}
{ci: Strip back down. Sparse.}
{ci: Slow the last line and leave space before "for Me."}
The stone rolled [D]back that morning
The [Db]grave gave way
I [B]rose to life
On [A]the third day
[G]Watch the sky[A]
{ci: (interlude)}
For you ... for Me

{comment: Interlude (reprise)}
{ci: Original sparse motif, once, then out.}
